312 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1025 0 R/E(Moisture \(interpretation key, not an independent detector\) \204 a crack does not necessarily stay air-filled; if water enters \(rain, mine drainage\), the same crack can flip from high resistance \(dry\) to low resistance \(water-filled, especially with dissolved minerals\). The co-located capacitive soil moisture sensor doesn't itself claim "crack" or "no crack" \204 its job is to tell the fuzzy logic stage which direction of resistivity anomaly to expect right now, so the system correctly interprets whichever direction the anomaly moves rather than being confused by it. This is a deliberately more precise claim than treating resistivity and moisture as two independent, equally-weighted pieces of evidence \204 state this explicitly, it's a genuine design strength.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

313 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1026 0 R/E(Temperature \204 corrects MEMS/electrode thermal drift and provides context for interpreting resistivity alongside moisture.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

314 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1027 0 R/E(Geological context \(Earth Engine: soil type, rock density\) \204 establishes the expected baseline resistivity range for this specific ground type, so a measured value is compared against a geology-informed expectation rather than an arbitrary universal threshold.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

315 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1028 0 R/E(These four combine into a single Crack/Ground-Anomaly Score \204 interpretable, rule-derived, in the same naming spirit as the Fuzzy Risk Index, never a binary "crack detected" claim. Feeds the ML residual model as one additional input feature; explicitly excluded from the Digital Twin, whose defining boundary is taking no live sensor input at all.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

