318 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 126 0 R/E(Not a mechanism-sensing tier \204 it provides positioning and a wide-area reference/calibration layer alongside the local sensing tiers, never a third local mechanism in the same category as Tiers 1-2.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

319 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1030 0 R/E(GNSS-based node georeferencing \204 a one-time registration device \(not continuous per-node GNSS\) captures accurate real-world coordinates and a baseline sensor reading at installation, enabling spatial mapping, physics-based influence modelling, InSAR feature sampling, and PI-STGNN graph construction. cumulative_displacement_since_baseline is tracked as a first-class quantity, since Knothe's function is inherently cumulative and must be compared against a like quantity, not a raw instantaneous reading. A low-cost module \(e.g. NEO-6M/NEO-M8N\) gives ~2-5m accuracy \204 sufficient for georeferencing but not sufficient to directly detect millimetre-scale subsidence movement. RTK GNSS \(centimetre-or-better\) is a costed future upgrade, not adopted now.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

320 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1031 0 R/E(InSAR \(Sentinel-1 via Copernicus/ASF HyP3\) \204 used for calibration and validation, never the real-time trigger, honestly scoped around its 6-12 day revisit limitation. Feeds both mining modes as a supplementary evidence channel, joining at the fusion stage, never independently triggering.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

321 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 126 0 R/T(4.3 Tier 3 \204 Reference Positioning and Satellite Calibration)/E(4.3 Tier 3 \204 Reference Positioning and Satellite Calibration)/Pg 22 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

322 0 obj
