330 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1035 0 R/E(Passive self-potential sensing \204 a genuinely different, passive geoelectrical technique for detecting water movement through a pathway.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

331 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1036 0 R/E(Mechanical/optical direct crack-gap sensors \(potentiometer extensometers, Time-of-Flight laser distance, Hall-effect/magnet pairs\) \204 valid, buildable alternatives to electrical resistivity; remain available if resistivity+moisture proves insufficient on the demo rig, but resistivity was chosen as primary since it doesn't require a crack to already exist at a precisely pre-known point.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

332 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 127 0 R/E(Sensor locations are determined using mine geometry, panel boundaries, angle-of-draw/influence zones, and reference areas outside the influence zone \204 never arbitrary spacing. Dense along the panel boundary/buffer ring \(where strain concentrates first per subsidence theory\), sparser interior, extra density at critical surface assets. Real-world node positions connect sensor observations to mine geometry, geological zones, influence relationships, and the Digital Twin \204 this geospatial anchoring is what makes every downstream physics calculation meaningful rather than abstract.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

333 0 obj
