endobj

346 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 128 0 R/T(5.2 The Core Architectural Fix \204 Evidence Fusion Replaces Hard Gating)/E(5.2 The Core Architectural Fix \204 Evidence Fusion Replaces Hard Gating)/Pg 24 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

347 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 128 0 R/E(The risk identified: the pipeline was originally wired as a serial AND-chain \204 each stage \(Kalman, fuzzy logic, spatial coherence\) could unilaterally suppress a reading before the next stage ever saw it. A true, developing event could be killed early if any single cheap stage under-reacted to it, even if later confirmed by other evidence.)/Pg 24 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

348 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 128 0 R/E(The fix: no single cheap algorithm retains permanent veto power. Kalman filtering, fuzzy logic, spatial coherence, and raw-residual monitoring now each produce independent evidence, combined into one weighted score. A sufficiently strong signal from any one channel alone can still escalate, even if others are inconclusive.)/Pg 24 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

349 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 128 0 R/E(Other fixes from the same review:)/Pg 24 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

350 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1037 0 R/E(Raw residual monitoring \204 the residual between the raw reading and the current filtered estimate \(raw - Kalman_estimate\) is tracked as a second, independent detection pathway that doesn't depend on the smoothed signal at all. Fixes the risk that a conservatively-tuned Kalman filter \(Q too small\) could lag behind and smooth away a genuinely sudden real event.)/Pg 24 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

351 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 129 0 R/Pg 25 0 R/A[960 0 R 0]/K[0]>>
endobj

352 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1038 0 R/E(Sensor health as a distinct state, not risk = 0 \204 a faulty/unresponsive sensor now reports a distinct UNKNOWN risk state \(a sentinel value\), never a false "confirmed safe." Evidence fusion treats sensor health as a gate on trust, not on risk \204 the one place a hard gate remains appropriate.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

353 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1039 0 R/E(Output renamed for honesty \204 the fuzzy stage's output is explicitly the Fuzzy Risk Index throughout code, comments, and documentation, never a "probability" \204 a fuzzy output like 0.92 would otherwise invite an unjustified statistical claim.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

354 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1040 0 R/E(Spatial coherence made continuous, not binary \204 a strict binary "escalate only if a neighbour also looks elevated" rule could incorrectly suppress the very first node to detect a genuinely developing, still-localised event. Now returns a continuous 0.0-1.0 spatialScore\(\) \(proportion of fresh, elevated neighbours\), one weighted input to evidence fusion rather than a gate \204 an isolated node can still escalate on the strength of its own evidence alone if strong enough.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

355 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 129 0 R/T(5.3 Kalman Filter \204 Full Mechanics)/E(5.3 Kalman Filter \204 Full Mechanics)/Pg 25 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

356 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(Problem it solves: a true, slowly-changing quantity \(e.g. actual ground tilt\) can only be observed through a noisy sensor reading. The filter combines a prediction \(based on the last estimate\) with the new noisy reading, weighted by trust in each, to produce a better estimate than either alone.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

357 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(State kept per sensor axis \(two numbers\): x \204 current best estimate of the true value; P \204 how uncertain that estimate is \(a variance\).)/Pg 25 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

358 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(Predict step: x_predicted = x_previous \(ground tilt doesn't jump randomly\). P_predicted = P_previous + Q, where Q is a small constant representing expected natural drift between readings.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

359 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(Update step \(when new raw reading z arrives\): K = P_predicted / \(P_predicted + R\) \204 the Kalman Gain \(0 to 1\), where R represents sensor noise \(estimated empirically by holding the sensor still and measuring scatter\). Then: x_new = x_predicted + K * \(z - x_predicted\), P_new = \(1 - K\) * P_predicted.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

360 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(Intuition for K: noisy sensor relative to prediction confidence -> K small, filter trusts its own prediction. Precise sensor -> K close to 1, filter trusts the new reading. A self-adjusting weighted average, not fixed-ratio smoothing.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

361 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(Worked example \(true tilt steady at 0.25 degrees\): raw readings 0.21, 0.31, 0.19, 0.28, 0.23, 0.34, 0.25 become filtered estimates approximately 0.21, 0.24, 0.22, 0.24, 0.24, 0.26, 0.26 \204 converges smoothly rather than tracking every noise spike.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

362 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 130 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/A[960 0 R 0]/K[0]>>
endobj

363 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 130 0 R/E(Terminology clarification: "filter" here means "correct/clean every sample," never "remove some samples." Exactly one output estimate per input reading, always \204 nothing is ever dropped at this stage.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

364 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 130 0 R/E(Honest limitation: if Q is set too small, the filter becomes overconfident and lags behind a genuinely sudden real event. If R is set too small, the filter over-trusts noisy raw readings. Mitigations: always log the raw reading alongside the filtered estimate \(never only filtered\); estimate R empirically per sensor before deployment; choose Q deliberately based on the fastest real event that must be tracked; document this as a known limitation rather than presenting the filter as infallible.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

365 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 130 0 R/T(Final firmware code \204 kalman_filter.h:)/E(Final firmware code \204 kalman_filter.h:)/Pg 26 0 R/K[3]>>
