411 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 132 0 R/T(5.4 Fuzzy Logic \204 Full Mechanics)/E(5.4 Fuzzy Logic \204 Full Mechanics)/Pg 28 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

412 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(Problem it solves: avoid a hard cutoff \(e.g. "tilt rate >= 0.3 deg/day = danger"\) that treats 0.29 and 0.31 as categorically different, and combine several differently-scaled/differently-meaning signals into one interpretable score.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

413 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(Step A - Fuzzification: each input is converted into overlapping degrees of membership in named categories via triangular/trapezoidal shapes \204 e.g. LOW membership = 1.0 at 0.0 deg/day, dropping to 0.0 at 0.3 deg/day; MODERATE peaking at 1.0 at 0.3 deg/day; HIGH rising from 0.0 at 0.3 deg/day. A reading of 0.35 deg/day might come out as LOW=0.0, MODERATE=0.75, HIGH=0.25.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

414 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(Step B - Rule evaluation: simple IF-THEN rules combine memberships across signals, e.g. "IF tilt_rate is HIGH AND vibration is SUSTAINED THEN risk is HIGH." AND = minimum of memberships; same-category-from-multiple-rules combine = maximum.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

415 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(Step C - Defuzzification: the combined fuzzy result converts back to one crisp number via a weighted average across representative centre values, e.g. risk_score = \(LOW*0.15 + MODERATE*0.5 + HIGH*0.9\) / \(sum of activations\).)/Pg 28 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

416 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 132 0 R/T(5.5 Spatial Coherence \204 Full Mechanics)/E(5.5 Spatial Coherence \204 Full Mechanics)/Pg 28 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

417 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(At prototype scale \(2-3 nodes\): a direct comparison \204 if a node's risk score is elevated AND at least one physically nearby neighbour's risk score is also elevated within the same recent time window, escalate as spatially consistent; else suppress and log locally as an isolated, likely non-subsidence event. Deliberately the simplest correct case of a rule that generalises upward, not a hardcoded 2-node assumption.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

418 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(At full-scale \(dozens of nodes\): generalises into a cellular-automaton propagation check \204 comparing observed risk-score patterns against propagation rules derived from angle-of-draw physics, since a genuine subsidence bowl should spread across neighbours in a physically consistent way an isolated fault or local disturbance would not.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

419 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 132 0 R/T(5.6 Evidence Fusion \204 Full Mechanics)/E(5.6 Evidence Fusion \204 Full Mechanics)/Pg 28 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

420 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(Runs on the gateway; replaces the old hard AND-gate. Combines Fuzzy Risk Index, spatial score, and raw-residual spike flag into one weighted evidence score, with an explicit rule that a sufficiently strong single signal can escalate on its own, and an explicit sensor-health gate.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

421 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 133 0 R/Pg 29 0 R/A[960 0 R 0]/K[0]>>
endobj

422 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 133 0 R/E(5.7 Dual-Rate Logging \(Solving the Data-Scarcity/False-Negative Risk\))/Pg 29 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

423 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 133 0 R/E(A pure "only transmit/store when abnormal" design leaves no record of what "normal" looks like over time \204 no negative examples, no baseline to compare a suspicious period against. The adopted fix: dual-rate logging, applied independently of the escalation decision \204 every Kalman-filtered reading is always logged locally at a steady low rate \(e.g. one summary per minute\) as a continuous baseline, and whenever the fuzzy/spatial stages flag a concern, logging/transmission switches to a much higher rate for a window around the event. Both raw and filtered values, plus risk score and escalation flag, are stored together at all times \204 filtering never means discarding data, only ever choosing the rate of attention.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

424 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 133 0 R/T(5.8 Hybrid GNN Triggering \204 Event-Gated + Scheduled Background)/E(5.8 Hybrid GNN Triggering \204 Event-Gated + Scheduled Background)/Pg 29 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

425 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 133 0 R/E(The gap identified and fixed: if the GNN only ever runs when fuzzy logic and spatial checks flag something, any case where those cheaper stages under-flag a genuinely developing but slow, borderline pattern means the GNN never gets a chance to catch exactly what it exists to catch.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

426 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 133 0 R/E(The fix \204 hybrid triggering: \(1\) event-triggered runs whenever fuzzy logic and spatial coherence flag a concern \(efficiency-driven path, unchanged\), plus \(2\) a periodic low-frequency background run over the full recent stored window of data, regardless of whether anything was flagged \204 a safety net for slow, subtle patterns, at small bounded extra compute cost.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

