457 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 136 0 R/E(A B&P region has PHSR = High. That tells us the area has high inherent susceptibility \204 it doesn't mean "collapse is happening right now." Now imagine mining state changes: before, extraction = 20%, pillars largely intact; later, extraction = 40%, several pillars removed, goaf expanded. Geological parameters haven't changed at all \204 PHSR = unchanged \204 but CURRENT STRUCTURAL STATE = changed. This is why PHSR should be treated as a baseline susceptibility layer, not the entire live risk calculation.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

